== Navigation and coverage source families ==

High-priority source families include:

* Wikipedia Contents and subject directories;
* Portal:Systems science and portal directories;
* Vital articles;
* Meta-Wiki's 1,000- and 10,000-topic cross-Wikipedia lists;
* categorization, category/list/navigation guidance;
* WikiProject Portals, portal statistics, and criticism/failure-mode pages;
* Wikipedia administration, maintenance, Village Pump, dashboard, Articles for Creation, Requested articles, and Stub systems;
* contribution/newcomer/help/directories categories;
* Wikipedia community, history, academic studies, bibliographies, controversy/censorship and contributor-safety cases;
* lists of Wikipedias, wiki communities, and online encyclopedias;
* sister-project mission boundaries such as Wikisource and Wikinews.

The durable URL ledger is maintained in [[BITwiki:Research references]] rather than duplicated across every design note.

== Core lessons currently extracted ==

=== Navigation plurality ===
No one taxonomy does all jobs. Contents, portals, categories, outlines, lists, glossaries, indices, semantic queries, graphs, and Core/Vital sets are complementary views.

=== Accessibility is architectural ===
Simple English demonstrates that reader accessibility can be treated as a systematic editorial target rather than an afterthought. BITwiki should go further by exposing progressive technical depth inside one coherent corpus instead of cloning entire subject trees.

=== Contribution pathways matter ===
Wikipedia's newcomer surfaces distinguish reading, learning to edit, asking for help, creating an account, improving existing material, creating a first article, requesting missing articles, and joining maintenance/community work. BITwiki needs similarly clear contributor routes, adapted for humans + agents and its own provenance/review model.

=== Self-administration is a separate plane ===
Administration, maintenance, proposals, technical discussion, content requests, drafts, quality review, and project policy need obvious project-facing navigation without being mixed into subject Domains.

=== Portals are expensive when manually duplicated ===
Portal proliferation and hidden subpage forests are a maintenance failure mode. BITwiki should prefer smaller numbers of useful portals with query-driven content and automatic validation.

=== Coverage priority is not ontology ===
Vital/core lists are useful because they make missing or weak coverage visible without pretending importance is an Entity type or Domain.

== Governance and security research ==

Track controversy patterns such as vandalism, capture, brigading, state pressure, legal risk, privacy, conflict-of-interest, misinformation, governance abuse, and automation failures. Separate content risk from contributor risk and infrastructure risk.

See [[BITwiki:Sensitive topic scope research]].

== Research discipline ==

* Distinguish policy/guideline from essay, proposal, historical page, article, or external criticism.
* Prefer primary project documentation and academic literature for architectural claims.
* Treat Wikipedia as evidence, not specification.
* Track failures as carefully as successful patterns.
* Do not equate scale with quality.
* Do not assume English Wikipedia conventions generalize everywhere.
* Do not study language editions merely because they are different languages; prioritize materially different editorial/governance/accessibility patterns.
* Do not turn every discovered distinction into a BITwiki namespace, Domain, Entity type, Property, or portal.
* Convert recurring comparative observations into structured data when the schema is mature enough.

